  "causebase_summary": "Institute of Public Works Engineering Australasia (NSW Division) Ltd (IPWEA NSW & ACT) is a professional association for public works and local government engineering professionals operating in New South Wales and the Australian Capital Territory. It delivers accredited qualifications, short courses and workshops as a Registered Training Organisation (RTO 90174) and provides NSW Government‑subsidised training via Smart and Skilled (318282). IPWEA NSW & ACT hosts technical events, forums and conferences — including a 2026 Public Works AI Forum and a Development Engineering Forum — and undertakes advocacy and policy activities. Participation options described include joining as a member, registering for and attending events, and enrolling in accredited or short courses. CauseBase does not have sufficient descriptive evidence in this release to identify direct service beneficiaries beyond the members and public works professionals named in the sources.",
